// What is happening here?
// ============================================================
// 1. Each vertex stores a linked list of neighboring vertices.
// 2. Every neighbor has a weight, meaning the cost to travel there.
// 3. Dijkstra checks the lowest-cost path first.
// 4. It keeps updating distances until the shortest route to all vertices is known.
// 5. The result gives the shortest route and total weight.

